      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess this makes it slower? Reading any APIC register except TPR/PPR/ISR/IRR now requires vmexit, and even worse, switching from pKVM to the host and back?\n\nMaybe we could instead sync those host-emulated register values from the host\u0027s apic page to the pKVM\u0027s one in the vCPU run loop, so that the guest can still read them without vmexit?\n\nOr perhaps none of those registers are _read_ (not just written) by guests in any hot paths in practice? But looks like, for instance, in Linux guests at least APIC_TMR is read in ioapic_ack_level(), i.e. as a part of handling any level-triggered interrupt?",
      "revId": "abff39daee3244a313bc37e76ab93b7711bd1067",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ce36ae64_6c6d1ac2",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
